.TH DT-FILTER 1 "August 2026" "dirtoo tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dt-filter \- evaluate dirtoo filter expressions against paths
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dt-filter
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I EXPRESSION
[\fIPATH\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Parse and apply a dirtoo filter DSL
.I EXPRESSION
to the listed paths (or paths read from the environment as documented in
.BR \-\-help ).
Useful for scripting and testing filter predicates without the GUI.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show full help, including expression syntax notes.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH FILTER LANGUAGE
Examples:
.PP
.nf
  *.png
  size:>1M type:file
  width:>=1920
  contains:hello
.fi
.PP
See the dirtoo GUI filter help and project documentation for the complete
language.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dirtoo (1),
.BR dt-copy (1),
.BR dt-move (1),
.BR dt-rename (1),
.BR dt-rm (1),
.BR dt-mkdir (1),
.BR dt-filter (1)
